    "content": "To file a claim for up to $2,500 from the Cash App class-action lawsuit (alleging data breaches in 2022/2023), eligible users must submit a claim form via the official settlement site, CashAppSecuritySettlement.com, by November 18, 2024. Claims require documentation of unauthorized transactions, stolen funds, or related fees. CashAppSecuritySettlement.com Steps to File a Cash App Settlement Claim: Verify Eligibility: You must have had a Cash App account at some point between August 23, 2018, and August 20, 2024, and experienced unauthorized, fraudulent transactions or related losses. Gather Documentation: Collect proof of losses, such as bank statements, emails to/from Cash App, or police reports. Complete the Claim Form: Visit CashAppSecuritySettlement.com to submit your claim electronically. CashAppSecuritySettlement.com Submit by Deadline: The final deadline to submit your claim form is November 18, 2024. Potential Compensation: Out-of-Pocket Losses: Up to $2,500 per user for documented fraudulent transactions or fees. Lost Time: Compensation for lost time, up to 3 hours at $25/hour. If you did not receive a notice and are unsure of your eligibility, you can still submit a claim through the official portal by filling in your account details, including your username or \"$Cashtag\". official portal",
